Here are the form test cases, organized so you can run them in order and record results. Unless stated otherwise, set the contact's **Country** first, then enter the phone in **Business Phone**. "Blank" means Country is empty. Check **saved** values in a view or Advanced Find, not on the form, since the form always shows the formatted version.

**Setup checks**

| ID | AC | Steps | Expected result |
|---|---|---|---|
| S1 | — | Open any contact; in the console (ClientApiWrapper frame) look for `ContactPhoneManager:` messages | No `libphonenumber is not loaded` warning, no errors |
| S2 | — | Open a contact with Power Apps Monitor running | `ContactPhoneManager.onLoad` runs without an error |

**Form load (display only)**

| ID | AC | Precondition | Steps | Expected result |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| L1 | AC7 | Stored `+12245221234` | Open the contact | Shows `+1 (224) 522-1234` |
| L2 | AC7 | Stored `+442079460958` | Open the contact | Shows `+44 20 7946 0958` |
| L3 | AC7 | Stored `+12245221234` | Open, change nothing, run `Xrm.Page.data.entity.getIsDirty()`, then navigate away | Returns `false`; no unsaved-changes prompt. If `true`, set `FORMAT_ON_LOAD = false` |
| L4 | AC7 | Stored `+12245221234` | Change Job Title only, run `Xrm.Page.data.entity.getDataXml()` | Only Job Title is in the XML; phone fields aren't sent |
| L5 | AC7 | Stored `+12245221234` | Change Job Title, save, check the stored phone | Still `+12245221234` |

