**Invalid entry: error and blocked save**

Each should show *"Phone number must contain a valid country code and telephone number."* on the field, and clicking Save should be blocked.

| ID | AC | Country | Enter | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| I1 | AC13 | Blank | `12345` | Fewer than 7 digits |
| I2 | AC13, AC14 | United States | `555-12` | Fewer than 7 digits |
| I3 | AC4 | Blank | `2245221234` | No country code, and no Country to infer it |
| I4 | — | Blank | `7123 4567` | Same, for a non-US number |
| I5 | — | Blank | `123-456-7890` | Not a real number with any country code |
| I6 | — | Blank | `+1234567890` | Too short for a +1 number |
| I7 | — | United States | `abc-defg` | No digits |

**Error clearing and save flow**

| ID | AC | Steps | Expected result |
|---|---|---|---|
| E1 | AC15 | Country US: enter `12345`, then change to `224-522-1234` | Error appears, then clears immediately |
| E2 | AC14 | Enter `12345`, click Save | Save blocked; error stays visible until corrected |
| E3 | AC8 | Save a valid number and stay on the form | Field shows the formatted version again after save |
| E4 | — | Clear an existing phone number and save | Saves as empty, no error |
| E5 | — | Contact with an old invalid phone (e.g. `555-1234`): change only Job Title and save | Save succeeds; the untouched phone doesn't block it |
| E6 | — | Country blank: enter `7123 4567` (error), set Country to Costa Rica, re-enter the number | Error clears; shows `+506 7123 4567` |

**Other forms and conditions**

| ID | AC | Steps | Expected result |
|---|---|---|---|
| F1 | AC12 | Click a formatted phone number | Click-to-call opens the dialer as before |
| F2 | — | Repeat V1 and I1 on every Contact form, including Quick Create | Same results on each form |
| F3 | — | Repeat V1 and I1 in the mobile app | Same results |
| F4 | — | Bulk edit two contacts and set a phone | No errors on open; entry is validated and formatted |
| F5 | — | User with read-only phone fields saves a contact that has an old invalid phone | Save succeeds; no blocking error |

Run L3 first, because its result decides the `FORMAT_ON_LOAD` setting. If a case fails, capture the console output or Monitor trace before changing anything.
